    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read the cost panels",
      "description": "Scope notes for the cost and API-comparison panels.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 90
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Cost panel scope**\n\n- **Active Direct-GPU Electricity Cost** is a *marginal* figure: only the energy the serving GPUs draw while requests are active. It excludes the host baseline (platform + CPU + idle GPUs) and hardware cost.\n- **Equivalent Remote API Workload Cost** prices the observed token flow at configured provider list rates (processed input, cached input, output) using the planning FX rate. It is a counterfactual, not a bill, and assumes the provider would hit the same cache behaviour; model capability is not equalised.\n- For the **all-in electricity** view use **Whole-Host Electricity Cost** and the Host Cost Today/Week/Month panels; that series already contains the idle baseline.\n- Measured production windows: whole-host electricity was within about 10% of the off-peak API-equivalent, while active-GPU energy alone was roughly half of it. The marginal panel is the right lens for incremental decisions; the host panels are the right lens for the true running cost.",
        "code": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        }
      },
      "targets": []
    },
    {
      "title": "Active Serving Profile",
      "description": "Profile reported by the exporter. The atx-dual profile has two independent llamAmpere replicas and unchanged Muse.",
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "max by (profile) (ai_serving_profile_info)",
          "legendFormat": "{{profile}}",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 96
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Replica Health",
      "description": "One series per configured replica, identified by model, physical GPU, GPU UUID, and exporter backend.",
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "max by (host_id, model, gpu, gpu_uuid, replica) (ai_replica_up{host_id=~\"$host_id\",model=~\"$model\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{model}} GPU {{gpu}} UUID {{gpu_uuid}} ({{replica}})",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
